WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.884
In analytical modeling the grain question remains
essential A fact

00:00:05.911 --> 00:00:11.453
table represents measurable events Before adding
columns state exactly what one

00:00:11.479 --> 00:00:16.920
fact row means A star schema connects the fact table
directly to

00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:22.673
descriptive dimensions This often makes analytical
queries easier to understand

00:00:24.403 --> 00:00:30.063
A snowflake design normalizes some dimensions into
related sub-dimensions That can

00:00:30.089 --> 00:00:35.673
reduce redundancy but increases the number of joins
Neither pattern

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:41.560
removes the need to define grain For our clinic
example one possible

00:00:41.586 --> 00:00:46.220
fact grain is one appointment-service line That
sentence tells us what each

00:00:46.247 --> 00:00:50.352
fact row represents and which measures keys and
dimensions can belong there

00:00:52.186 --> 00:00:55.817
Always define fact grain before designing an
analytical table
